# {{distribution}}

A [dvf](https://pypi.org/project/dvf-framework/) plugin. {{summary}}

The {{kind}} `{{name}}` is registered through the `{{group}}` entry point group, so dvf
finds it as soon as this package is installed. The generated component works as written; replace
its logic with your own and keep the tests passing.

## Develop

```bash
python -m venv .venv
. .venv/bin/activate          # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -e ".[test]"
pytest
dvf plugins list --kind {{kind}}
```

## Use

```yaml
{{usage}}
```

`dvf validate-config` checks the settings against the component's `Config` model, and
`dvf schema config` includes them in the JSON Schema for editor autocomplete.

## Compatibility

The component declares `dvf_plugin_api = "{{plugin_api}}"`. dvf refuses to load it, with a
clear message in `dvf plugins list`, when its plugin API is outside that range. Widen the range
after testing with a newer dvf, and keep `dvf-framework{{dvf_requirement}}` in `pyproject.toml`
in step.

## Publish

```bash
pip install build twine
python -m build
twine check dist/*
twine upload dist/*           # or publish from CI with PyPI Trusted Publishing
```

Name public packages `dvf-<organization>-<purpose>` and keep component names namespaced
(`acme.vat_number_valid`) so they never collide with future built-ins.
